 "admissions_overview": {
  "summary": "Admission to public university degree programmes in Kenya is mainly through the Kenya Universities and Colleges Central Placement Service (KUCCPS), based on performance in the Kenya Certificate of Secondary Education (KCSE). Applicants choose programmes on the KUCCPS online portal, where a cluster weight is calculated from their KCSE subjects, and placement is competitive and depends on the vacancies available. Universities also admit self-sponsored students directly and publish their own intakes and minimum requirements.",
  "official_url": "https://kuccps.net",
  "notes": "Application windows, the list of programmes and the number of places, and the cluster subjects and weights for each programme change every year. Check kuccps.net and the admissions page of the university each year."
 },
